From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:39:35 -0400
Subject: feat: shortcuts the user can change (S-91)

The Shortcuts block on chrome://settings/stedding becomes editable
(docs/features/shortcuts.md Z5, Z10-Z23). Every command a shipped chord
reaches has a row: Add records a chord, x takes one off, a switch turns
a command's keys off, Reset and Reset all put the defaults back, and a
search field and a group menu narrow the rows (Z5, Z22). The chords live
in Local State under stedding.shortcuts.user, keyed by stable names
(Z10), and apply at once in every window through one overlay that the
views table, the Mac's menu and coded tables, the command bar, the held
recent-tabs and extensions chords and the toolbar tooltips all read
(Z11, Z18). A chord another row has is named and Replace moves it
(Z12); the shipped tables bind no chord twice (Z13); system,
text-editing, macOS and extension shortcuts are refused (Z14, Z15);
fixed rows are read-only (Z16); the row-number and Space chords switch
off as one row (Z17), and a menu under the Space row lets the two
sets trade keys or moves one to Ctrl-Cmd, Alt+Shift on Windows (Z23,
GitHub issue 13); the recorder gets the browser's own keys (Z19); a
user chord beats a later default (Z20); the divergences and notes keep
describing the shipped binary (Z21).

Why: docs/PRODUCT.md section 12 puts shortcut customisation at 1.0
(BACKLOG S-91, ROADMAP M10); the read-only reference was the last step
short of it.
Removable when: never as a feature; the overlay hunks in Chromium's
accelerator tables, menu dispatcher and BrowserView go only if Chromium
ships its own desktop shortcut remapping that Stedding adopts.
